{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787865414278279433,"compiled_state":{"alias":"daughterly-agitative-ocelot","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"34135a418ac00352ef69b883ecace74cadd78d43e6390170b1db3ba82d147412","event_uuid":"86f2fdac-57ca-4737-b33a-2f71545c2bda","position":{"commit_sha":"5a81f000bb90629a6c2438c7c14dd57a159ac4d8","position":"1787858559072112001-86f2fdac-57ca-4737-b33a-2f71545c2bda"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6937291bfbd1189a00cbd9a157873872f7166d0b0e33026904903d2a6a109e75","event_uuid":"2d6d2cc5-efb8-4627-90ea-ebdbc4c9d8be","position":{"commit_sha":"099e44612307acd7f3916032767cdb21ea884d7b","position":"1787860192268545001-2d6d2cc5-efb8-4627-90ea-ebdbc4c9d8be"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787858559072112001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Summary\n\n`list_tickets` against this store can terminate with `MCP request failed: Transport closed` and\nno structured error payload — the caller cannot tell whether the query was invalid, the server\nfailed, or the response was simply too large.\n\n## Observed (parallel Copilot CLI session)\n\n    list_tickets -> MCP server 'rebar': MCP request failed: Transport closed\n\nThe reporter attributes it to response size, noting that `ready_tickets` and `bridge_fsck`\n'needed disk-spill just to return'.\n\n## Corroborating datum from a different client\n\nIn a Claude Code session the same tool SUCCEEDED but returned **219,815 characters**, which\nexceeded the client's token budget and had to be spilled to a file. So the server can emit\npayloads far beyond what a client can absorb, and it does so without pagination or a size guard.\n\n## Candidate causes — deliberately NOT collapsed into one\n\nThree are live and this ticket should not presume among them:\n1. **Response size** — the reporter's hypothesis, supported by the 219KB datum.\n2. **BigInt serialization** (`unreal-milky-sloth`) — a JS client can fail on out-of-JS-range\n   integers; a failure during serialization can look like a dropped transport.\n3. **A deploy cutover** — the mcp container was replaced at 18:54:29Z\n   (`nemophilic-prettyish-cockroach`), which orphans live sessions.\n\nThese produce similar client-visible symptoms and must be separated by evidence before a fix.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The cause is identified and distinguished from the two sibling tickets above.\n- [ ] A large result is bounded — pagination, an explicit limit, or a documented cap — rather\n      than emitted at unbounded size.\n- [ ] Exceeding any limit produces a STRUCTURED, actionable error, never a bare transport close.\n- [ ] Regression coverage exercises a store large enough to trip the previous behaviour.\n\n- [ ] **LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE.** `list_tickets` and `ready_tickets` called through the deployed endpoint return results (or a structured limit error) with no transport close.\n      Evidence must be OBSERVED against the deployed server at\n      `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` and recorded in a ticket comment naming\n      the tool(s) called, the arguments, and the actual response. A passing local test is\n      NOT sufficient, and neither is a merged change: the container must have redeployed\n      and served the call. This exists because a fix here was previously reported complete\n      on the strength of a merge while the deployed behaviour was still broken.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["mcp","transport","scale"],"ticket_id":"494b-2dd3-e9d3-4fb0","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP list_tickets can close the transport on a large store, with no structured error","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["86f2fdac-57ca-4737-b33a-2f71545c2bda","2d6d2cc5-efb8-4627-90ea-ebdbc4c9d8be"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787865414278279433,"uuid":"d719d716-1e21-450e-8072-1e3bc51e2c0d"}